{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-26463","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-30782","text":"RRABBIT runbook — bringing the stack up, and proving it"}]},{"id":"blk-26464","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30783","text":"The spec ("},{"id":"spn-30784","marks":["code"],"text":"docs/spec/README.md"},{"id":"spn-30785","text":") records "},{"id":"spn-30786","marks":["italic"],"text":"what was found and why"},{"id":"spn-30787","text":". This file is the other half: the commands, the port map, and the measurements that settle an argument. It exists because every session so far has re-derived the same six facts before it could start work."}]},{"id":"blk-26465","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30788","text":"Nothing here is optional folklore — each rule below is a trap someone already fell into, with the section of the spec that records it."}]},{"id":"blk-26466","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-30789","text":"1. The port map"}]},{"id":"blk-26467","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30790","text":"Five servers, and they are not interchangeable."}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-26469","spans":[{"id":"spn-30791","text":"port"}]},{"id":"blk-26470","spans":[{"id":"spn-30792","text":"what"}]},{"id":"blk-26471","spans":[{"id":"spn-30793","text":"started by"}]},{"id":"blk-26472","spans":[{"id":"spn-30794","text":"notes"}]}],"id":"blk-26468","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-26473","spans":[{"id":"spn-30795","marks":["bold"],"text":"8911"}]},{"id":"blk-26474","spans":[{"id":"spn-30796","text":"vite dev — the shell from source, HMR"}]},{"id":"blk-26475","spans":[{"id":"spn-30797","marks":["code"],"text":"npm run m0"}]},{"id":"blk-26476","spans":[{"id":"spn-30798","text":"iterate here"}]}],[{"id":"blk-26477","spans":[{"id":"spn-30799","marks":["bold"],"text":"8912"}]},{"id":"blk-26478","spans":[{"id":"spn-30800","text":"compositor-proxy — native applications"}]},{"id":"blk-26479","spans":[{"id":"spn-30801","marks":["code"],"text":"npm run proxy"}]},{"id":"blk-26480","spans":[{"id":"spn-30802","text":"needs the addon and a GL device"}]}],[{"id":"blk-26481","spans":[{"id":"spn-30803","marks":["bold"],"text":"8913"}]},{"id":"blk-26482","spans":[{"id":"spn-30804","marks":["code"],"text":"bridge.py"},{"id":"spn-30805","text":" — the "},{"id":"spn-30806","marks":["bold"],"text":"built"},{"id":"spn-30807","text":" shell + the seven tubes"}]},{"id":"blk-26483","spans":[{"id":"spn-30808","marks":["code"],"text":"python3 bridge.py 8913"}]},{"id":"blk-26484","spans":[{"id":"spn-30809","text":"stdlib only; this is what the distro ships"}]}],[{"id":"blk-26485","spans":[{"id":"spn-30810","marks":["bold"],"text":"8905"}]},{"id":"blk-26486","spans":[{"id":"spn-30811","text":"PARKVPS "},{"id":"spn-30812","marks":["code"],"text":"vpsd/api.py"},{"id":"spn-30813","text":" — the machines"}]},{"id":"blk-26487","spans":[{"id":"spn-30814","marks":["code"],"text":"python3 vpsd/api.py --port 8905"}]},{"id":"blk-26488","spans":[{"id":"spn-30815","text":"QEMU lives behind this"}]}],[{"id":"blk-26489","spans":[{"id":"spn-30816","marks":["bold"],"text":"8890"}]},{"id":"blk-26490","spans":[{"id":"spn-30817","text":"RAVIO "},{"id":"spn-30818","marks":["code"],"text":"bridge.py"},{"id":"spn-30819","text":" — the sky road"}]},{"id":"blk-26491","spans":[{"id":"spn-30820","marks":["code"],"text":"python3 bridge.py --port 8890"}]},{"id":"blk-26492","spans":[{"id":"spn-30821","text":"its MACHINES rail reads 8905"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-26493","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30822","text":"All are in the repo-root "},{"id":"spn-30823","marks":["code"],"text":".claude/launch.json"},{"id":"spn-30824","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-30825","marks":["code"],"text":"rrabbit-m0"},{"id":"spn-30826","text":", "},{"id":"spn-30827","marks":["code"],"text":"rrabbit-bridge"},{"id":"spn-30828","text":", "},{"id":"spn-30829","marks":["code"],"text":"parkvps"},{"id":"spn-30830","text":", "},{"id":"spn-30831","marks":["code"],"text":"ravio"},{"id":"spn-30832","text":")."}]},{"id":"blk-26494","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30833","marks":["bold"],"text":"`--allow-origin` must name the page's port, not the proxy's."},{"id":"spn-30834","text":" It now defaults to "},{"id":"spn-30835","marks":["bold"],"text":"both"},{"id":"spn-30836","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-30837","marks":["code"],"text":"8911,8913"},{"id":"spn-30838","text":") and "},{"id":"spn-30839","marks":["code"],"text":"proxy.sh"},{"id":"spn-30840","text":" prints what it allowed — a list needs "},{"id":"spn-30841","marks":["code"],"text":"patches/proxy-cli-multi-origin.md"},{"id":"spn-30842","text":", because upstream wrote the value into the header verbatim and "},{"id":"spn-30843","marks":["code"],"text":"Access-Control-Allow-Origin"},{"id":"spn-30844","text":" may name exactly one origin, so a comma list refused every entry."}]},{"id":"blk-26495","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30845","text":"If you serve the shell from anywhere else, say so, or the launch fails with a CORS refusal that reads exactly like the proxy being down:"}]},{"id":"blk-26496","kind":"code","language":"bash","text":"RRABBIT_ALLOW_ORIGIN=http://127.0.0.1:9000 npm run proxy"},{"id":"blk-26497","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30846","marks":["bold"],"text":"Restart the proxy between page reloads."},{"id":"spn-30847","text":" A proxy session outlives the page and is keyed by "},{"id":"spn-30848","marks":["code"],"text":"compositorSessionId"},{"id":"spn-30849","text":", so a reload joins a session whose client is gone — a window that never appears, with nothing in any log. Spec §21.1."}]},{"id":"blk-26498","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-30850","text":"2. Launching a window"}]},{"id":"blk-26499","kind":"code","language":"js","text":"window.__launch('/tandr-tr4-foot')     // any path in proxy/applications.json"},{"id":"blk-26500","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30851","marks":["code"],"text":"?remote=…"},{"id":"spn-30852","text":" fires during "},{"id":"spn-30853","marks":["bold"],"text":"boot"},{"id":"spn-30854","text":", which makes it useless for anything that has to be armed "},{"id":"spn-30855","marks":["italic"],"text":"before"},{"id":"spn-30856","text":" the first frame — a probe on the decoder, say. "},{"id":"spn-30857","marks":["code"],"text":"__launch"},{"id":"spn-30858","text":" is the same one launch path, on demand."}]},{"id":"blk-26501","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30859","marks":["code"],"text":"proxy/applications.json"},{"id":"spn-30860","text":" is schema-validated with "},{"id":"spn-30861","marks":["code"],"text":"additionalProperties:false"},{"id":"spn-30862","text":". An extra annotation field makes compositor-proxy "},{"id":"spn-30863","marks":["bold"],"text":"throw before opening the socket"},{"id":"spn-30864","text":" — the whole proxy goes down for one stray key."}]},{"id":"blk-26502","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30865","text":"It ships in the build now ("},{"id":"spn-30866","marks":["code"],"text":"shipApplications()"},{"id":"spn-30867","text":" in "},{"id":"spn-30868","marks":["code"],"text":"vite.config.ts"},{"id":"spn-30869","text":"), so the built menu is the real list rather than "},{"id":"spn-30870","marks":["code"],"text":"NATIVE_MIRROR"},{"id":"spn-30871","text":". Add a program in one place."}]},{"id":"blk-26503","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-30872","text":"Which programs actually open, measured 2026-08-13"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-26505","spans":[{"id":"spn-30873","text":""}]},{"id":"blk-26506","spans":[{"id":"spn-30874","text":""}]}],"id":"blk-26504","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-26507","spans":[{"id":"spn-30875","marks":["code"],"text":"xterm"},{"id":"spn-30876","text":", "},{"id":"spn-30877","marks":["code"],"text":"glxgears"}]},{"id":"blk-26508","spans":[{"id":"spn-30878","text":"open (XWayland)"}]}],[{"id":"blk-26509","spans":[{"id":"spn-30879","marks":["code"],"text":"foot · tr4"}]},{"id":"blk-26510","spans":[{"id":"spn-30880","text":"opens (guest, via waypipe)"}]}],[{"id":"blk-26511","spans":[{"id":"spn-30881","marks":["code"],"text":"gnome-text-editor"}]},{"id":"blk-26512","spans":[{"id":"spn-30882","text":"opens "},{"id":"spn-30883","marks":["bold"],"text":"only"},{"id":"spn-30884","text":" with "},{"id":"spn-30885","marks":["code"],"text":"DBUS_SESSION_BUS_ADDRESS"},{"id":"spn-30886","text":" pointed at a nonexistent path"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-26513","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30887","text":"A GTK application inherits "},{"id":"spn-30888","marks":["code"],"text":"DBUS_SESSION_BUS_ADDRESS"},{"id":"spn-30889","text":", finds the copy already running on your desktop, hands off and exits 0 in under 100 ms. It looks exactly like a crash and it is a feature. Any single-instance GTK app needs the same entry. "},{"id":"spn-30890","marks":["code"],"text":"WAYLAND_DISPLAY"},{"id":"spn-30891","text":" is "},{"id":"spn-30892","marks":["italic"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-30893","text":" the problem — "},{"id":"spn-30894","marks":["code"],"text":"launchApplication"},{"id":"spn-30895","text":" sets it to the proxy's own socket, last, over "},{"id":"spn-30896","marks":["code"],"text":"process.env"},{"id":"spn-30897","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-26514","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-30898","text":"3. Measurements that settle arguments"}]},{"id":"blk-26515","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30899","text":"These are the probes that actually decided things. Prefer them to reasoning."}]},{"id":"blk-26516","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-30900","text":"Is a frame reaching the browser, and what shape is it?"}]},{"id":"blk-26517","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30901","text":"Monkey-patch the decoder from the console "},{"id":"spn-30902","marks":["italic"],"text":"before"},{"id":"spn-30903","text":" launching:"}]},{"id":"blk-26518","kind":"code","language":"js","text":"var RealVD = window.VideoDecoder\nwindow.VideoDecoder = function (init) {\n  var d = new RealVD({ output: f => { console.log(f.format, f.codedWidth, f.codedHeight,\n                                                  f.visibleRect, f.allocationSize()); init.output(f) },\n                       error: init.error })\n  return d\n}\nwindow.VideoDecoder.isConfigSupported = RealVD.isConfigSupported.bind(RealVD)"},{"id":"blk-26519","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30904","text":"Wrapping "},{"id":"spn-30905","marks":["code"],"text":"VideoFrame.prototype.copyTo"},{"id":"spn-30906","text":" and logging the returned "},{"id":"spn-30907","marks":["code"],"text":"PlaneLayout[]"},{"id":"spn-30908","text":" gives the per-plane offset and stride — which is how you tell a padded decode from a stride bug. This single probe is what found §23."}]},{"id":"blk-26520","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-30909","text":"Which way is a window up?"}]},{"id":"blk-26521","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30910","text":"Inject a texture that is asymmetric "},{"id":"spn-30911","marks":["italic"],"text":"by construction"},{"id":"spn-30912","text":" through the real upload path, and read the glass back:"}]},{"id":"blk-26522","kind":"code","language":"js","text":"var cv = new OffscreenCanvas(W, H), cx = cv.getContext('2d')\ncx.fillStyle = '#ff0000'; cx.fillRect(0, 0, W, H / 2)      // FIRST rows\ncx.fillStyle = '#0000ff'; cx.fillRect(0, H / 2, W, H / 2)\nscene['image/bitmap']({ size: { width: W, height: H },\n                        pixelContent: await createImageBitmap(cv) }, renderState)"},{"id":"blk-26523","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30913","text":"Red at the top of the sign means texel row 0 renders at the top, which means a window is upright."}]},{"id":"blk-26524","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30914","marks":["bold"],"text":"`simple-shm` cannot settle orientation."},{"id":"spn-30915","text":" Its pattern is mirror-symmetric about its own midline, so no sample of it can decide the flip — "},{"id":"spn-30916","marks":["code"],"text":"__orient"},{"id":"spn-30917","text":" correctly reports "},{"id":"spn-30918","marks":["code"],"text":"inconclusive"},{"id":"spn-30919","text":". Do not try to read it by eye either."}]},{"id":"blk-26525","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-30920","text":"Where is a control on the cockpit?"}]},{"id":"blk-26526","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30921","text":"Compute it. "},{"id":"spn-30922","marks":["bold"],"text":"Do not scan with `window.__dashAt`"},{"id":"spn-30923","text":" — it calls "},{"id":"spn-30924","marks":["code"],"text":"hooks.dashHit"},{"id":"spn-30925","text":", which is "},{"id":"spn-30926","marks":["italic"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-30927","text":" pure: it toggles the ST&RT menu and knocks the gear stick, so a scan closes the menu it is measuring and you conclude the menu will not stay open. ("},{"id":"spn-30928","marks":["code"],"text":"dash.hit()"},{"id":"spn-30929","text":" is pure; "},{"id":"spn-30930","marks":["code"],"text":"hooks.dashHit"},{"id":"spn-30931","text":" is the layer that acts on it.)"}]},{"id":"blk-26527","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30932","text":"The dash is drawn in a 1920×1080 design box ("},{"id":"spn-30933","marks":["code"],"text":"dash.js"},{"id":"spn-30934","text":", "},{"id":"spn-30935","marks":["code"],"text":"layout()"},{"id":"spn-30936","text":"):"}]},{"id":"blk-26528","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"s = W / 1920                         // W, H are the canvas size\nty = H - 1080 * s                    // + the hidden-slide term when it is sliding\nclientX = design.x * s\nclientY = design.y * s + ty"},{"id":"blk-26529","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30937","marks":["code"],"text":"__dash()"},{"id":"spn-30938","text":" reports every rectangle in design space ("},{"id":"spn-30939","marks":["code"],"text":"startRect"},{"id":"spn-30940","text":", "},{"id":"spn-30941","marks":["code"],"text":"startMenu"},{"id":"spn-30942","text":"), and "},{"id":"spn-30943","marks":["code"],"text":"startMenuRect"},{"id":"spn-30944","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-30945","marks":["code"],"text":"startRows"},{"id":"spn-30946","text":" in "},{"id":"spn-30947","marks":["code"],"text":"dash.js"},{"id":"spn-30948","text":" derive the rows from the list length. One conversion, no probing, no side effects."}]},{"id":"blk-26530","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-30949","text":"Logging out — the power key, and why it can refuse"}]},{"id":"blk-26531","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30950","text":"The cockpit's bottom-left corner is now two controls: "},{"id":"spn-30951","marks":["bold"],"text":"POWER"},{"id":"spn-30952","text":" at design "},{"id":"spn-30953","marks":["code"],"text":"x=22"},{"id":"spn-30954","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-30955","marks":["bold"],"text":"ST&RT"},{"id":"spn-30956","text":" moved right to "},{"id":"spn-30957","marks":["code"],"text":"x=80"},{"id":"spn-30958","text":". Power opens a confirm plate; the one row on it posts "},{"id":"spn-30959","marks":["code"],"text":"bridge.py /api/logout"},{"id":"spn-30960","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-26532","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30961","marks":["bold"],"text":"Nothing in the browser can end the session."},{"id":"spn-30962","text":" "},{"id":"spn-30963","marks":["code"],"text":"window.close()"},{"id":"spn-30964","text":" will not close the last window of a kiosk, and the page has no session to end. The chain is:"}]},{"id":"blk-26533","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"shell POST /api/logout  ->  bridge reads the pidfile  ->  SIGTERM the browser\n     ->  `wait` in rrabbit-session returns  ->  the script exits  ->  the greeter"},{"id":"blk-26534","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30965","text":"The pidfile ("},{"id":"spn-30966","marks":["code"],"text":"/tmp/rrabbit-browser.pid"},{"id":"spn-30967","text":", "},{"id":"spn-30968","marks":["code"],"text":"RRABBIT_BROWSER_PIDFILE"},{"id":"spn-30969","text":") holds "},{"id":"spn-30970","marks":["code"],"text":"<pid> <comm>"},{"id":"spn-30971","text":". Both fields are checked before anything is signalled: pids are reused, and a session that died without clearing its file would otherwise arm this endpoint against whatever inherited the number. "},{"id":"spn-30972","marks":["code"],"text":"comm"},{"id":"spn-30973","text":" is recorded by "},{"id":"spn-30974","marks":["code"],"text":"rrabbit-session"},{"id":"spn-30975","text":" "},{"id":"spn-30976","marks":["italic"],"text":"at launch"},{"id":"spn-30977","text":" rather than assumed here, because "},{"id":"spn-30978","marks":["code"],"text":"firefox"},{"id":"spn-30979","text":" may be a wrapper and then the waited-on process is not called "},{"id":"spn-30980","marks":["code"],"text":"firefox"},{"id":"spn-30981","text":" at all."}]},{"id":"blk-26535","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30982","marks":["bold"],"text":"A bridge you started by hand REFUSES, and that is correct"},{"id":"spn-30983","text":" — there is no session, and a shell that reached for the nearest Firefox would kill the one you are developing in. The refusal is printed on the plate itself:"}]},{"id":"blk-26536","kind":"code","language":"bash","text":"curl -s -X POST http://127.0.0.1:8913/api/logout"},{"head":[{"id":"blk-26538","spans":[{"id":"spn-30984","text":"answer"}]},{"id":"blk-26539","spans":[{"id":"spn-30985","text":"what it means"}]}],"id":"blk-26537","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-26540","spans":[{"id":"spn-30986","marks":["code"],"text":"409 no session to end — nothing wrote …"}]},{"id":"blk-26541","spans":[{"id":"spn-30987","text":"served outside a session; expected on a workstation"}]}],[{"id":"blk-26542","spans":[{"id":"spn-30988","marks":["code"],"text":"409 pid N is X, not Y"}]},{"id":"blk-26543","spans":[{"id":"spn-30989","text":"stale pidfile, or the wrong process inherited the pid"}]}],[{"id":"blk-26544","spans":[{"id":"spn-30990","marks":["code"],"text":"409 pid N is not running"}]},{"id":"blk-26545","spans":[{"id":"spn-30991","text":"the session died without clearing its file"}]}],[{"id":"blk-26546","spans":[{"id":"spn-30992","marks":["code"],"text":"200 {ok, pid, signal}"}]},{"id":"blk-26547","spans":[{"id":"spn-30993","text":"signalled — if the page is still there, the browser ignored it"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-26548","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30994","marks":["code"],"text":"__dash().powerWhy"},{"id":"spn-30995","text":" is the sentence on the plate; "},{"id":"spn-30996","marks":["code"],"text":"__m1().lastLogout"},{"id":"spn-30997","text":" carries the status code and pid behind it. "},{"id":"spn-30998","marks":["bold"],"text":"Any message left on that plate is a fault"},{"id":"spn-30999","text":", successes included — a logout that worked takes the page with it."}]},{"id":"blk-26549","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-31000","text":"The target has no devtools — use the report endpoint"}]},{"id":"blk-26550","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31001","text":"The only machine that matters runs a kiosk Firefox with no address bar and no console, so a diagnostic you cannot reach there is not a diagnostic."}]},{"id":"blk-26551","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"RRABBIT_URL_EXTRA=\"remote=/notes,/firefox&report=45\"   # in rrabbit-session\ngrep -a REPORT /tmp/rrabbit-bridge.log | tail -1 | sed 's/^REPORT //' | python3 -m json.tool"},{"id":"blk-26552","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31002","marks":["code"],"text":"?remote="},{"id":"spn-31003","text":" launches at boot — "},{"id":"spn-31004","marks":["bold"],"text":"comma-separated, so it opens more than one"},{"id":"spn-31005","text":" — and "},{"id":"spn-31006","marks":["code"],"text":"?report=<secs>"},{"id":"spn-31007","text":" posts to "},{"id":"spn-31008","marks":["code"],"text":"bridge.py /api/report"},{"id":"spn-31009","text":", which prints it. "},{"id":"spn-31010","marks":["bold"],"text":"No clicking"},{"id":"spn-31011","text":", which matters — see the click note under §5."}]},{"id":"blk-26553","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31012","marks":["bold"],"text":"The report REPEATS, so `tail -1` is \"what is true now\"."},{"id":"spn-31013","text":" It used to fire once, which meant every question about a "},{"id":"spn-31014","marks":["italic"],"text":"window"},{"id":"spn-31015","text":" had to be asked by guessing, before the page loaded and from a shell script, how long it would take to open one — and anything needing two programs up at the same time was a race against a timer set in the past. It now re-arms after each POST settles (one in flight, never a queue). Set "},{"id":"spn-31016","marks":["code"],"text":"report=10"},{"id":"spn-31017","text":" while iterating."}]},{"id":"blk-26554","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31018","marks":["bold"],"text":"Do not `: >` the bridge log to clear it."},{"id":"spn-31019","text":" bridge.py holds it open at its current offset, so truncating punches a NUL hole that the next write skips past — and "},{"id":"spn-31020","marks":["code"],"text":"grep"},{"id":"spn-31021","text":" then treats the file as binary and silently matches nothing. Use "},{"id":"spn-31022","marks":["code"],"text":"grep -a"},{"id":"spn-31023","text":", or restart the bridge."}]},{"id":"blk-26555","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31024","text":"The fields that actually discriminate, and what each rules out:"}]},{"id":"blk-26556","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31025","marks":["code"],"text":"views: []"},{"id":"spn-31026","text":" with "},{"id":"spn-31027","marks":["code"],"text":"appStates: open"},{"id":"spn-31028","text":" means the signalling socket connected and "},{"id":"spn-31029","marks":["bold"],"text":"no surface ever existed"},{"id":"spn-31030","text":" — a completely different fault from a view that exists with "},{"id":"spn-31031","marks":["code"],"text":"hasBuffer:false"},{"id":"spn-31032","text":". That pair is what found §27.7 after two turns of guessing."}]},{"id":"blk-26557","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31033","marks":["code"],"text":"errors"},{"id":"spn-31034","text":" is bounded at 20 and keeps the "},{"id":"spn-31035","marks":["bold"],"text":"first"},{"id":"spn-31036","text":", not the last: the tube poll can emit hundreds of identical failures, and the error that explains a failure is almost always the first one."}]},{"id":"blk-26558","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-31037","text":"Does the quad carry a picture?"}]},{"id":"blk-26559","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31038","marks":["code"],"text":"state.decodes"},{"id":"spn-31039","text":" is "},{"id":"spn-31040","marks":["bold"],"text":"declared and never incremented"},{"id":"spn-31041","text":" (spec §19.5). It reads as \"no frames decoded\" and means nothing. Use a GL readback:"}]},{"id":"blk-26560","kind":"code","language":"js","text":"var c = document.querySelector('#gl'), g = c.getContext('webgl'), px = new Uint8Array(4)\ng.readPixels(x, c.height - y, 1, 1, g.RGBA, g.UNSIGNED_BYTE, px)"},{"id":"blk-26561","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31042","text":"or "},{"id":"spn-31043","marks":["code"],"text":"__views()"},{"id":"spn-31044","text":" for "},{"id":"spn-31045","marks":["code"],"text":"hasBuffer"},{"id":"spn-31046","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-31047","marks":["code"],"text":"rect"},{"id":"spn-31048","text":", or "},{"id":"spn-31049","marks":["code"],"text":"__orient()"},{"id":"spn-31050","text":" for the flip."}]},{"id":"blk-26562","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-31051","text":"Is the built bundle the shell you tested?"}]},{"id":"blk-26563","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31052","text":"Minification mangles class names, so "},{"id":"spn-31053","marks":["code"],"text":"constructor.name === 'Surface'"},{"id":"spn-31054","text":" checks are dead in the shipped artifact and nothing errors (spec §18.3). Identify by shape ("},{"id":"spn-31055","marks":["code"],"text":"isSurface"},{"id":"spn-31056","text":", "},{"id":"spn-31057","marks":["code"],"text":"positionerState"},{"id":"spn-31058","text":"), and grep the bundle for the strings your fix depends on:"}]},{"id":"blk-26564","kind":"code","language":"bash","text":"npm run build\ngrep -c \"video/h264\\|UNPACK_FLIP_Y_WEBGL\\|resetState\" dist/assets/shell-*.js"},{"id":"blk-26565","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31059","marks":["bold"],"text":"Testing that the bundle runs is not testing that its features still work in it."}]},{"id":"blk-26566","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-31060","text":"4. The shared GL context — the rule the whole shell turns on"}]},{"id":"blk-26567","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31061","text":"three.js and Greenfield draw into "},{"id":"spn-31062","marks":["bold"],"text":"one"},{"id":"spn-31063","text":" WebGL context. Upstream that context is Greenfield's alone, so its passes set only what they use and inherit defaults for everything else. Here they inherit whatever three left switched on."}]},{"id":"blk-26568","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31064","marks":["code"],"text":"fenceScenePasses()"},{"id":"spn-31065","text":" in "},{"id":"spn-31066","marks":["code"],"text":"shell.js"},{"id":"spn-31067","text":" is the one seam that fixes this, and it wraps all three of "},{"id":"spn-31068","marks":["code"],"text":"Scene"},{"id":"spn-31069","text":"'s entry points — "},{"id":"spn-31070","marks":["code"],"text":"video/h264"},{"id":"spn-31071","text":", "},{"id":"spn-31072","marks":["code"],"text":"image/bitmap"},{"id":"spn-31073","text":", "},{"id":"spn-31074","marks":["code"],"text":"image/png"},{"id":"spn-31075","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-26569","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31076","text":"Two things about it that are not negotiable:"}]},{"id":"blk-26570","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-26572","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31077","marks":["bold"],"text":"Per-pass, not around `renderer.render`."},{"id":"spn-31078","text":" The passes run in a microtask that"}]}],"id":"blk-26571","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-26573","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31079","marks":["code"],"text":"render()"},{"id":"spn-31080","text":" queues, so state set outside it is only still true by luck."}]},{"id":"blk-26574","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-26576","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31081","marks":["bold"],"text":"`renderer.resetState()` on the way out"},{"id":"spn-31082","text":", or three keeps drawing the road on"}]}],"id":"blk-26575","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-26577","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31083","text":"Greenfield's settings."}]},{"id":"blk-26578","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31084","text":"If you ever add a fourth entry point to "},{"id":"spn-31085","marks":["code"],"text":"Scene"},{"id":"spn-31086","text":", it goes in the fence. Spec §23."}]},{"id":"blk-26579","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-31087","text":"5. Driving a FreeBSD guest with no browser at all"}]},{"id":"blk-26580","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31088","text":"The T&R image is graphical, and for a long time the only way to look at it was a browser pointed at PARKVPS. It is not. QEMU will hand you the framebuffer and take keystrokes directly:"}]},{"id":"blk-26581","kind":"code","language":"bash","text":"cd PARKVPS\npython3 vpsd/vps.py screenshot tr4 /tmp/g.ppm && magick /tmp/g.ppm /tmp/g.png\npython3 vpsd/vps.py type tr4 driver @tab driver @ret      # log in at the greeter\npython3 vpsd/vps.py type tr4 @2                           # a key the shell reads\npython3 vpsd/vps.py click tr4 72 702                      # the ST&RT button"},{"id":"blk-26582","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31089","text":"The guest has a "},{"id":"spn-31090","marks":["code"],"text":"usb-tablet"},{"id":"spn-31091","text":", which is "},{"id":"spn-31092","marks":["bold"],"text":"absolute"},{"id":"spn-31093","text":" — a pixel on the screenshot is a pixel to click, with no pointer warping and no relative drift. Screenshot, read the coordinate off the picture, click it."}]},{"id":"blk-26583","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31094","marks":["bold"],"text":"This reaches places ssh cannot."},{"id":"spn-31095","text":" ssh tells you what a shell says is true; "},{"id":"spn-31096","marks":["code"],"text":"screenshot"},{"id":"spn-31097","text":" shows you the screen — the greeter before anyone has logged in, a session that failed to start, an X server on the wrong VT. "},{"id":"spn-31098","marks":["code"],"text":"ps aux | grep firefox"},{"id":"spn-31099","text":" returning rows does not mean anything is on the display."}]},{"id":"blk-26584","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31100","marks":["code"],"text":"magick"},{"id":"spn-31101","text":" is present on this host; there is no python "},{"id":"spn-31102","marks":["code"],"text":"PIL"},{"id":"spn-31103","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-26585","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-31104","text":"Getting a new shell build into a running guest"}]},{"id":"blk-26586","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31105","text":"The image ships "},{"id":"spn-31106","marks":["code"],"text":"dist/"},{"id":"spn-31107","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-31108","marks":["code"],"text":"bridge.py"},{"id":"spn-31109","text":" to "},{"id":"spn-31110","marks":["code"],"text":"/usr/local/share/rrabbit/"},{"id":"spn-31111","text":" and runs them under Firefox kiosk. Replacing the bundle in a running instance takes about a second and does not need an image rebuild:"}]},{"id":"blk-26587","kind":"code","language":"bash","text":"cd RRABBIT && npm run build\ntar czf - dist | ssh $OPTS park@127.0.0.1 \\\n  'sudo rm -rf /usr/local/share/rrabbit/dist.new &&\n   sudo mkdir -p /usr/local/share/rrabbit/dist.new &&\n   sudo tar xzf - -C /usr/local/share/rrabbit/dist.new --strip-components=1 &&\n   sudo mv /usr/local/share/rrabbit/dist /usr/local/share/rrabbit/dist.old &&\n   sudo mv /usr/local/share/rrabbit/dist.new /usr/local/share/rrabbit/dist'"},{"id":"blk-26588","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31112","text":"Then "},{"id":"spn-31113","marks":["bold"],"text":"reboot the guest"},{"id":"spn-31114","text":" — "},{"id":"spn-31115","marks":["code"],"text":"service sddm restart"},{"id":"spn-31116","text":" orphans an Xorg on VT 9, after which every new display server "},{"id":"spn-31117","marks":["italic"],"text":"and"},{"id":"spn-31118","text":" the greeter crash in ~22 ms, which presents exactly like the session you just installed being broken."}]},{"id":"blk-26589","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31119","text":"Confirm you are running what you built, by hash, not by looking:"}]},{"id":"blk-26590","kind":"code","language":"bash","text":"ssh $OPTS park@127.0.0.1 'sha256 -q /usr/local/share/rrabbit/dist/assets/shell-*.js'\nsha256sum dist/assets/shell-*.js"},{"id":"blk-26591","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31120","marks":["bold"],"text":"Replace `dist`, never overlay it."},{"id":"spn-31121","text":" The 0.4 image carried "},{"id":"spn-31122","marks":["bold"],"text":"five"},{"id":"spn-31123","text":" orphan "},{"id":"spn-31124","marks":["code"],"text":"shell-*.js"},{"id":"spn-31125","text":" bundles from earlier builds. Same class of bug as the addons manifest (spec §19): an overlay leaves files that then look like they belong."}]},{"id":"blk-26592","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-31126","text":"Native programs inside the guest — the host's proxy, over the network"}]},{"id":"blk-26593","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31127","text":"The image carries no compositor-proxy and cannot (no node, no gstreamer, no "},{"id":"spn-31128","marks":["code"],"text":"/dev/dri"},{"id":"spn-31129","text":"). It does not need its own: under QEMU user-mode networking the host answers on the default gateway and SLIRP maps it to the host's "},{"id":"spn-31130","marks":["bold"],"text":"loopback"},{"id":"spn-31131","text":", so "},{"id":"spn-31132","marks":["code"],"text":"--bind-ip=127.0.0.1"},{"id":"spn-31133","text":" is already reachable from the guest at "},{"id":"spn-31134","marks":["code"],"text":"10.0.2.2:8912"},{"id":"spn-31135","text":" with nothing exposed."}]},{"id":"blk-26594","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31136","marks":["code"],"text":"rrabbit-session"},{"id":"spn-31137","text":" appends "},{"id":"spn-31138","marks":["code"],"text":"?proxy=http://10.0.2.2:8912"},{"id":"spn-31139","text":" "},{"id":"spn-31140","marks":["bold"],"text":"only when the default route is `10.0.2.2`"},{"id":"spn-31141","text":" — anywhere else that is someone else's router. "},{"id":"spn-31142","marks":["code"],"text":"RRABBIT_PROXY"},{"id":"spn-31143","text":" overrides in either direction (empty string = never)."}]},{"id":"blk-26595","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31144","text":"This also needs "},{"id":"spn-31145","marks":["code"],"text":"publicBaseURL"},{"id":"spn-31146","text":" in "},{"id":"spn-31147","marks":["code"],"text":"patches/proxy-cli-multi-origin.md"},{"id":"spn-31148","text":": the proxy hands back a "},{"id":"spn-31149","marks":["code"],"text":"signalURL"},{"id":"spn-31150","text":" built from "},{"id":"spn-31151","marks":["code"],"text":"--base-url"},{"id":"spn-31152","text":", and a static value would tell the guest to connect to "},{"id":"spn-31153","marks":["italic"],"text":"itself"},{"id":"spn-31154","text":". Check it landed by grepping the proxy log for the address the client came back on:"}]},{"id":"blk-26596","kind":"code","language":"bash","text":"grep \"New signaling connection\" proxy.log      # must say 10.0.2.2 for a guest"},{"id":"blk-26597","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31155","text":"It also needs the "},{"id":"spn-31156","marks":["bold"],"text":"client-side"},{"id":"spn-31157","text":" correction in "},{"id":"spn-31158","marks":["code"],"text":"shell.js"},{"id":"spn-31159","text":": the proxy builds each application's protocol-channel URL from the static "},{"id":"spn-31160","marks":["code"],"text":"--base-url"},{"id":"spn-31161","text":" with no request in scope, so it tells a guest to connect to "},{"id":"spn-31162","marks":["code"],"text":"127.0.0.1"},{"id":"spn-31163","text":" — itself. The shell rewrites the proxy's own "},{"id":"spn-31164","marks":["code"],"text":"/channel"},{"id":"spn-31165","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-31166","marks":["code"],"text":"/signal"},{"id":"spn-31167","text":" WebSocket URLs to the host it actually reached the proxy on. Server-side and client-side corrections carry "},{"id":"spn-31168","marks":["italic"],"text":"different transports"},{"id":"spn-31169","text":" (HTTP vs WebSocket); neither is redundant."}]},{"id":"blk-26598","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31170","marks":["bold"],"text":"Working"},{"id":"spn-31171","text":": a host application renders on the guest's road ("},{"id":"spn-31172","marks":["code"],"text":"docs/m12-host-app-in-guest.png"},{"id":"spn-31173","text":")."}]},{"id":"blk-26599","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-31174","text":"Where it shows up"}]},{"id":"blk-26600","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31175","text":"RAVIO's "},{"id":"spn-31176","marks":["bold"],"text":"MACHINES"},{"id":"spn-31177","text":" rail (shift into "},{"id":"spn-31178","marks":["bold"],"text":"P — the drive-in"},{"id":"spn-31179","text":", "},{"id":"spn-31180","marks":["code"],"text":"g"},{"id":"spn-31181","text":" cycles gears) lists "},{"id":"spn-31182","marks":["code"],"text":"PARKVPS /api/fleet"},{"id":"spn-31183","text":" and opens each guest as a tab at "},{"id":"spn-31184","marks":["code"],"text":"http://127.0.0.1:8905/desktop/<name>"},{"id":"spn-31185","text":". That URL is a plain page and can be opened on its own — which is the quickest way to see a guest's screen in a browser, and it does not need RAVIO to be running."}]},{"id":"blk-26601","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-31186","text":"6. Harness traps (agent-browser)"}]},{"id":"blk-26602","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-26604","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31187","marks":["bold"],"text":"Isolated session + software GL, or you measure nothing:"}]}],"id":"blk-26603","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-26605","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31188","marks":["code"],"text":"--args \"--use-angle=swiftshader,--enable-unsafe-swiftshader,--disable-gpu-vsync,--disable-frame-rate-limit\""},{"id":"spn-31189","text":". "},{"id":"spn-31190","marks":["code"],"text":"--args"},{"id":"spn-31191","text":" is "},{"id":"spn-31192","marks":["bold"],"text":"ignored if the daemon is already running"},{"id":"spn-31193","text":" — "},{"id":"spn-31194","marks":["code"],"text":"agent-browser close --all"},{"id":"spn-31195","text":" first, or set "},{"id":"spn-31196","marks":["code"],"text":"AGENT_BROWSER_ARGS"},{"id":"spn-31197","text":" in the environment, which survives."}]},{"id":"blk-26606","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-26608","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31198","marks":["bold"],"text":"A blocked profile stays blocked."},{"id":"spn-31199","text":" After repeated context losses Chrome"}]}],"id":"blk-26607","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-26609","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31200","text":"answers "},{"id":"spn-31201","marks":["code"],"text":"Web page caused context loss and was blocked"},{"id":"spn-31202","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-31203","marks":["italic"],"text":"every"},{"id":"spn-31204","text":" later "},{"id":"spn-31205","marks":["code"],"text":"getContext('webgl')"},{"id":"spn-31206","text":" in that profile returns null. A fresh "},{"id":"spn-31207","marks":["code"],"text":"--session"},{"id":"spn-31208","text":" name is a fresh profile."}]},{"id":"blk-26610","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-26612","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31209","marks":["bold"],"text":"RRABBIT survives SwiftShader; RAVIO does not."},{"id":"spn-31210","text":" RRABBIT (4 canvases) renders"}]}],"id":"blk-26611","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-26613","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31211","text":"headless. RAVIO (5) loses its context on load, which kills the dash canvas that owns gear changes and key handling — so "},{"id":"spn-31212","marks":["code"],"text":"g"},{"id":"spn-31213","text":" does nothing and the app looks broken. It is the harness. Do not report it as a RAVIO fault without a real-GPU browser (spec §\"READ FIRST\" in the start-menu notes)."}]},{"id":"blk-26614","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-26616","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31214","marks":["bold"],"text":"`screenshot` takes an absolute path."},{"id":"spn-31215","text":" A relative one is written relative to"}]}],"id":"blk-26615","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-26617","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31216","text":"the daemon's cwd, not yours, and the command still prints "},{"id":"spn-31217","marks":["code"],"text":"✓ saved"},{"id":"spn-31218","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-26618","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-26620","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31219","marks":["bold"],"text":"`click` takes a selector, not coordinates."},{"id":"spn-31220","text":" "},{"id":"spn-31221","marks":["code"],"text":"click 1120 737"},{"id":"spn-31222","text":" matches nothing,"}]}],"id":"blk-26619","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-26621","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31223","marks":["bold"],"text":"exits 0 and dispatches no event"},{"id":"spn-31224","text":". A coordinate click is "},{"id":"spn-31225","marks":["code"],"text":"mouse move X Y"},{"id":"spn-31226","text":" → "},{"id":"spn-31227","marks":["code"],"text":"mouse down"},{"id":"spn-31228","text":" → "},{"id":"spn-31229","marks":["code"],"text":"mouse up"},{"id":"spn-31230","text":". Prove the event arrived before trusting it."}]},{"id":"blk-26622","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-26624","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31231","marks":["bold"],"text":"`console` output is cumulative across page loads"},{"id":"spn-31232","text":", so a stale error from a"}]}],"id":"blk-26623","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-26625","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-31233","text":"previous load reads as a live one."}]}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaierabvfnddka5c5bcez7a42eha5jno56tguilqn2l473bhu5h4ykrg6a","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}